                {
                  "formattedValue": "16 November 2026 update: Full original fixed-city theorem passed source-first, independent and adversarial review. The exact normalized hard-area ODE has unique global positive classical trajectories; beta>2alpha gives the stated explicit all-site/all-positive-initial persistence bound. The asymmetric three-city example stays between1/4096 and2047/2048. The literal unrestricted2007alpha>1 collapse alternative fails; the later stochastic founding model and convergence are outside scope. Aldous's protected-neighborhood mechanism and Ferudun's directly overlapping qualitative two-city inference receive prior credit; no firstness is claimed. One ordinary original exact-arithmetic diagnostic passed; all229 source files and30directories stayed unchanged. Native1.0.0 is actually printed. No repair, narrowing or qualifying follow-up. Page preparing; canonical blank until live verification. Evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/9d9c389718f51d9f2dd8abf603c84169cdabb9ea/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-clearance-23393139-20261116.json\n\nEarlier inventory note:\nComplete five-page native manuscript and 192-line controlling TeX acquired with checksum-bound original files. Native creation: 15 October 2026 at 11:02:16 UTC. Independent source-first scope and adversarial INITIALs are frozen; full reviews and root examination remain pending. No scientific disposition or public page approved; canonical remains blank. Source evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/65256bfa6661c2965226bfaa1ca65ce6c551904f/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-source156-adoption-20261116.json\n\nEarlier inventory note:\nPublished paper record with checksum-bound manuscript; deep review still required.",
